// inference and scoring have to agree about the new rank. `AST::unify_type` already decayed `T&` against
// a non-pointer argument, so before todo/A13c it named an instance that `argument_fit` then rejected -
// harmless only because the disagreement had nowhere to show
//
// **a second overload is present on purpose.** with one candidate, matching rule 2 wins without
// consulting types at all, so a disagreement between the two rules is invisible. that is exactly how the
// t_read_through bug survived

function bump<T>(T& $v) : T { return $v; }
function bump(bool $b, bool $c) : bool { return $b; }

echo bump(41);

int32 $named = 7;
echo bump($named);
